R\": true, \"CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC\": true, \"CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_BACKGROUND_TASKS\": true},\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-651-\t\t},\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-652-\t\tConfigDirEnv: \"CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR\", Log: w.Log,\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-653-\t})\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-654-}\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-655-\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-656-// parseResources applies --k8s-resources to the defaults. Keys: cpu and\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-657-// memory set the agent's requests, memory-limit its memory limit and\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-658-// ephemeral-storage its ephemeral-storage limit.\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-659-func parseResources(s string) (kube.Resources, error) {\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-660-\tr := kube.DefaultResources()\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-661-\tif strings.TrimSpace(s) == \"\" {\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-662-\t\treturn r, nil\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-663-\t}\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-664-\tfor _, kv := range strings.Split(s, \",\") {\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-665-\t\tk, v, ok := strings.Cut(strings.TrimSpace(kv), \"=\")\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-666-\t\tif !ok || v == \"\" {\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-667-\t\t\treturn r, fmt.Errorf(\"--k8s-resources: %q is not name=quantity\", kv)\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-668-\t\t}\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-669-\t\tswitch k {\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-670-\t\tcase \"cpu\", \"memory\":\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-671-\t\t\tr.Agent.Requests[k] = v\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-672-\t\tcase \"memory-limit\":\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-673-\t\t\tr.Agent.Limits[\"memory\"] = v\ninternal/servecmd/serve.go-674-\t\tcase \"ephemeral-storage\":\n# Role images on the Kubernetes executor (#245, #448)\n\nHow to turn on in-cluster role image builds for an `ard serve` that runs the\nKubernetes executor. With it on, a role that has a `Dockerfile` (the starter\nscanners and `reviewers/security-review`) runs on its own image instead of the\nplain agent image. See\n[docs/proposal.md: Executors and the Reaper](../proposal.md#executors-and-the-reaper)\nand [Delivery](../proposal.md#delivery).\n\nThe chart side is #448. ard serve uses it once #449 lands; until then the chart\nobjects exist and nothing creates builder pods.\n\n## What the chart creates\n\nWith `roleImages.enabled: true` and `executor.kind: k8s`:\n\n- the namespace `ard-build-<instance>` (or `roleImages.buildNamespace`), with\n  default-deny NetworkPolicies plus DNS and internet egress for builder pods,\n  a ResourceQuota and a LimitRange;\n- the `ard-build` ServiceAccount (no token) and a Role for ard serve: pods\n  create/delete/get/list, pods/log get, secrets create/delete;\n- a ValidatingAdmissionPolicy that admits only builder pods: one `buildkit`\n  container running exactly `roleImages.builder.image` as\n  `roleImages.builder.uid`, not privileged, no host namespaces, mounting only\n  the push Secret and its own Secret;\n- optionally an ExternalSecret for the push credential.\n\nThe build namespace enforces Pod Security **privileged** (and warns and audits\nat baseline): rootless BuildKit needs seccomp and AppArmor Unconfined to make\nuser namespaces. The admission policy is what keeps that namespace narrow.\n\n## 1. Create the push token\n\nghcr accepts pushes only from a classic personal access token (or\n`GITHUB_TOKEN` in Actions). A GitHub App token or a fine-grained PAT cannot\npush packages.\n\n1. As the account that owns `ghcr.io/<owner>`, create a classic token with\n   only `write:packages` (it implies `read:packages`). Give it an expiry and\n   note it in your calendar.\n2. Store it in the secret store the cluster reads, as one item with two\n   fields: `username` (the GitHub login) and `token`.\n\nNever paste the token into values files, the deployment repository or an\nissue.\n\n## 2. Allow the namespace in Argo CD\n\nThe deployment repository's AppProject must allow the build namespace as a\ndestination, next to the jobs namespace. The cluster-scoped kinds\n(`Namespace`, `ValidatingAdmissionPolicy`, `ValidatingAdmissionPolicyBinding`)\nare already allowed for the jobs namespace.\n\n## 3. Set the values\n\nIn the deployment repository's site values (or one instance's):\n\n```yaml\nsite:\n  roleImages:\n    enabled: true\n    repository: ghcr.io/<owner>/ard\n    pushSecret:\n      secretName: ard-role-image-push\n      externalSecret:\n        enabled: true\n        storeName: <store>\n        itemId: <item id>\n        itemTitle: ghcr role image push\n```\n\nTo create the Secret yourself instead, leave `externalSecret.enabled` false\nand create a `kubernetes.io/dockerconfigjson` Secret of that name in the build\nnamespace.\n\nKeep `roleImages.builder.image` at the chart's pin unless you are upgrading\nBuildKit; it must stay `<repository>@sha256:<digest>`.\n\n## 4. Make the packages public\n\nRole images are pulled with no `imagePullSecrets`, so each package must be\npublic. A new ghcr package under a user account starts private. After the\nfirst build of each role pushes `ghcr.io/<owner>/ard/<type>-<name>`:\n\n1. Open the package on GitHub (Your profile, Packages).\n2. Package settings, Danger Zone, Change visibility, Public.\n\nUntil a package is public, a job pod that uses it fails with `ImagePullBackOff`.\n\nDo not publish an image you may not redistribute. The `trufflehog` scanners\nare AGPL and stay off under the Kubernetes executor; do not enable them there.\n\n## 5. Check\n\n```sh\nkubectl get ns ard-build-<instance> --show-labels\nkubectl -n ard-build-<instance> get secret ard-role-image-push -o jsonpath='{.type}'\nkubectl get validatingadmissionpolicy ard-<instance>-build\n```\n\nThe Secret's type must be `kubernetes.io/dockerconfigjson`. Do not print its\ndata.\n\n## Rotate or turn off\n\n- **Rotate:** update the token in the store; the ExternalSecret refreshes\n  within `refreshInterval` (4h by default). Revoke the old token afterwards.\n- **Turn off:** set `roleImages.enabled: false`. Argo CD prunes the build\n  namespace and its Secret, and roles run on the agent image again.\n7-pod beside the old one would block on it. Pause: kubectl -n ard exec deploy/<name> -- touch\n8-/home/ard/.ard/pause/<owner>/<repo> (the kill switch; rm to resume).\n9-With executor k8s the pod gets its own ServiceAccount and a short-lived projected token (still no automount), and the\n10:--k8s-* settings as ARD_K8S_* env; it serves nothing, so there is no Service and no container port.\n11-With roleImages.enabled it also gets the build namespace, the builder image and uid, the role image repository and\n12:the push Secret's name (ARD_K8S_BUILD_*, ARD_K8S_BUILDER_*, ARD_K8S_ROLE_IMAGE_*; read by #449), never the credential.\n13-*/ -}}\n14-apiVersion: apps/v1\n15-kind: Deployment\n--\n69-              valueFrom: {secretKeyRef: {name: {{ .Values.githubApp.secretName }}, key: ARD_GITHUB_INSTALLATION_ID}}\n70-            - {name: ARD_GITHUB_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE, value: /var/run/ard/github-app/private-key.pem}\n71-            {{- if $k8s }}\n72:            - {name: ARD_K8S_NAMESPACE, value: {{ include \"ard-serve.jobsNamespace\" . }}}\n73:            - {name: ARD_K8S_INSTANCE, value: {{ $name }}}\n74:            - {name: ARD_K8S_POD_IMAGE, value: {{ $image | quote }}}\n75:            - {name: ARD_K8S_AGENT_IMAGE, value: {{ include \"ard-serve.agentImage\" . | quote }}}\n76-            {{- with .Values.jobs.resources }}\n77:            - {name: ARD_K8S_RESOURCES, value: {{ . | quote }}}\n78-            {{- end }}\n79-            {{- if include \"ard-serve.roleImages\" . }}\n80:            - {name: ARD_K8S_BUILD_NAMESPACE, value: {{ include \"ard-serve.buildNamespace\" . }}}\n81:            - {name: ARD_K8S_BUILDER_IMAGE, value: {{ .Values.roleImages.builder.image | quote }}}\n82:            - {name: ARD_K8S_BUILDER_UID, value: {{ .Values.roleImages.builder.uid | quote }}}\n83:            - {name: ARD_K8S_ROLE_IMAGE_REPOSITORY, value: {{ .Values.roleImages.repository | quote }}}\n84:            - {name: ARD_K8S_ROLE_IMAGE_PUSH_SECRET, value: {{ .Values.roleImages.pushSecret.secretName | quote }}}\n85-            {{- end }}\n86-            {{- with .Values.modelCredential }}{{ if .secretName }}\n87-            # The model credential ard serve forwards into each agent job's Secret (#434).\ninner_integration_test.go\nkind_integration_test.go\ntestdata\n(eval):1: no matches found: .ard/*/*/Dockerfile","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f535f0b-91e2-4cd6-a20e-142f0e47e2e5","uuid":"7d1053b6-fc70-4049-a1a1-2d1f528061f7","timestamp":"2026-11-26T08:33:52.301Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"client.go\nfake\nrest.go\nrest_test.go\ntypes.go\n30:type Client interface {\n31-\tCreatePod(ctx context.Context, ns string, p *Pod) (*Pod, error)\n32-\t// GetPod returns ErrNotFound when the pod does not exist.\n33-\tGetPod(ctx context.Context, ns, name string) (*Pod, error)\n34-\tListPods(ctx context.Context, ns, labelSelector string) ([]Pod, error)\n35-\t// DeletePod uses background propagation; a missing pod is not an error.\n36-\tDeletePod(ctx context.Context, ns, name string, graceSec int64) error\n37-\t// PodLogs follows the container log with timestamps. A zero sinceTime\n38-\t// starts at the beginning.\n39-\tPodLogs(ctx context.Context, ns, name, container string, sinceTime time.Time) (io.ReadCloser, error)\n40-\t// CreateSecret returns ErrConflict when the Secret exists.\n41-\tCreateSecret(ctx context.Context, ns string, s *Secret) error\n42-\t// DeleteSecret treats a missing Secret as success.\n43-\tDeleteSecret(ctx context.Context, ns, name string) error\n44-\tListEvents(ctx context.Context, ns, fieldSelector string) ([]Event, error)\n45-}\ninternal/executor/local/docker.go-19-\ninternal/executor/local/docker.go-20-// imageTag is a content-addressed tag: it changes when any file or mode in\ninternal/executor/local/docker.go-21-// the role directory changes.\ninternal/executor/local/docker.go:22:func imageTag(stage, role, roleDir string) (string, error