{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChREP6iagP85AHGuykfAu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0123v45TjLRY48FREtq2BFhE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work; mkdir -p .ard/449; ls .ard/449; cat > .ard/449/plan.md <<'EOF'\n# Plan for #449\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Steps\nFacts found in the code: `internal/executor/kube/kube.go` `Prepare` logs `kube.dockerfile_ignored` and sets `h.Image = e.o.AgentImage`; `kube.Options` has no build settings; `internal/servecmd/serve.go` `newKubeExecutor` builds `kube.Options` from the `--k8s-*` settings (`wiring.K8s`); the chart (#448) already passes `ARD_K8S_BUILD_NAMESPACE`, `ARD_K8S_BUILDER_IMAGE`, `ARD_K8S_BUILDER_UID`, `ARD_K8S_ROLE_IMAGE_REPOSITORY` and `ARD_K8S_ROLE_IMAGE_PUSH_SECRET` and a Role in the build namespace (pods create/delete/get/list, pods/log get, secrets create/delete). The #448 builder is a **pod** shape enforced by a ValidatingAdmissionPolicy (ServiceAccount `ard-build`, one container named `buildkit` running exactly the pinned image as the pinned uid, only the push Secret and the pod's own Secret mounted), not a batch Job; the chart has no Job RBAC. So the build is a pod, as in the issue's intent. Role Dockerfiles that use the agent image already declare `ARG AGENT_IMAGE=ard-agent:dev` / `FROM ${AGENT_IMAGE}` (`internal/roles/reviewers/security-review/Dockerfile`); the others use pinned `golang` bases. No role Dockerfile needs editing.\n\n1. `internal/executor/kube/api/types.go` and `fake/fake.go` (edit): confirm `PodStatus`/container state expose `terminated.message`, `exitCode` and `reason`; add whatever is missing (JSON fields only), and make the fake let a test script a builder pod's end state (phase, terminated message) and its logs. Reason: the build digest is read from the termination message and failures need the exit code.\n2. `internal/executor/kube/roleimage.go` (new): the role image builder.\n   - `type RoleImages struct { Namespace, BuilderImage, Repository, PushSecret string; BuilderUID int64; AgentBase string (default \"ghcr.io/albertcbrown/ard/agent:latest\"); Budget time.Duration (default 15m); Registry string (default \"https://ghcr.io\"); MaxContext int64 (default 512 KiB) }`; a new `Options.RoleImages *RoleImages` (nil = images off, keep `kube.dockerfile_ignored`). `New` validates fields and `executor.CheckImageRef(BuilderImage)`.\n   - `func (e *Executor) roleImage(ctx, j executor.Job) (ref string, err error)`:\n     a. Read the role directory from the controller clone at the pinned SHA, never the worktree: `git ls-tree -r -z <RoleSource.SHA> -- <RoleSource.Path>` in `j.RepoDir` for mode, blob id and relative path (use the existing git runner interface from `workspace.Options.Git` / `local.ExecGit`; read how `internal/executor/workspace` calls it). Reject symlinks (mode 120000) and submodules, and a missing `Dockerfile` in the listing.\n     b. Tag `h-<first 32 hex of sha256 over sorted \"mode path blobid\\n\" lines>`; include the base build-arg value in the hash input so changing `AgentBase` rebuilds. Repository `<Repository>/<stage-type>-<role>` where type is `scanners|triage|workers|reviewers` from `RoleSource.Path` (`.ard/<type>/<name>`); validate both segments against `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$`.\n     c. Registry check: anonymous pull token (`GET <Registry>/token?service=ghcr.io&scope=repository:<repo>:pull`), then `HEAD /v2/<repo>/manifests/<tag>` with OCI and Docker manifest Accept headers; 200 returns `Docker-Content-Digest`, so the ref is `<repo>@<digest>`. 401, 403 and 404 mean \"not built yet\" (a package that is still private looks the same), so go on to build. Other errors/5xx/timeouts fail the job as `registry check`. Use `Options.HTTP`.\n     d. Single-flight per tag (`map[string]*call` under `e.mu`) so concurrent jobs for one role share one build and one result.\n     e. Build: export the context with `git archive --format=tar <sha>:<path>` (cap at `MaxContext`; a larger context fails clearly), create a Secret in the build namespace holding it, then the builder pod copying the exact #448 admission shape (read `deploy/charts/ard-serve/templates/build-namespace.yaml` for volumes, uid, seccomp/AppArmor Unconfined, resources; do not edit it). Command: `buildctl-daemonless.sh build --frontend dockerfile.v0 --local context=/ctx --local dockerfile=/ctx --opt build-arg:AGENT_IMAGE=<AgentBase> --output type=image,name=<repo>:<tag>,push=true --metadata-file /dev/termination-log` (adapt flags to what the pinned BuildKit supports; the digest comes from `containerimage.digest`). Pod name `ard-build-<tag12>`, labels `app.kubernetes.io/instance`, `ard.dev/role-image`, restart never, `activeDeadlineSeconds` = Budget. Set the Secret's ownerReference to the pod after creation like `buildSecret` in `pod.go`.\n     f. Wait by polling `GetPod` every `Options.Poll` until Succeeded/Failed/deadline. Failure causes, each a typed error wrapping `executor.ErrInvalidJob`-independent sentinel `ErrRoleImageBuild`: `build failed (exit N): <last 20 log lines, redacted with internal/redact>`, `build timed out after <Budget>`, `builder pod not scheduled/admission denied: <create error>`, `no digest reported`. Always delete pod and Secret on exit with `context.WithoutCancel`.\n     g. Return `<repo>@sha256:...`; reject any digest that is not `sha256:` + 64 hex.\n3. `internal/executor/kube/kube.go` (edit `Prepare`): when `j.Dockerfile != \"\"` and `e.o.RoleImages != nil`, call `roleImage` **before** `WS.Prepare` (so a build failure leaves no worktree to discard) and set `h.Image` to the digest ref; otherwise keep the log line and `AgentImage`. Confirm `buildPod` in `internal/executor/kube/pod.go` uses `h.Image` for the agent container (and that `PodImage` stays for the pre/post containers); change it to if not. A build failure returns an error that the job runner records as the job failure cause. Add an `Image` field to the `kube.role_image` log line (job, ref, built or cached).\n4. `internal/servecmd/serve.go` (edit): add the five settings to the K8s settings struct and flag/env mapping following the existing `--k8s-*` / `ARD_K8S_*` pattern (build namespace, builder image, builder uid, role image repository, push secret). Role images are on only when the build namespace is set; then require the rest and `CheckImageRef` the builder image; pass `RoleImages` into `kube.Options`. Never read or log the push credential; only the Secret's name is used.\n5. `internal/executor/local/docker.go` (edit `ensureImage`): pass `--build-arg AGENT_IMAGE=<l.agentImage>` when the local executor has a configured agent image, otherwise rely on the Dockerfile default (`ard-agent:dev`), so the local executor keeps its locally built base. Add a test through the existing fake docker seam in `internal/executor/local` (see `agentimage_test.go`). Do not change the image tag hash.\n6. `docs/proposal.md` (edit): in the role Dockerfile bullet (~line 466) and the \"Role images\" bullet in Delivery (~line 584) replace \"k8s role images stay with #245\" and \"ard serve builds them from #449\" wording with the behaviour: built in the cluster by the controller at the pinned role SHA, tag `h-<hash>`, registry check, builder pod with budget, pod pinned by digest, controller-only requests, build context never from a PR worktree. Add to **Residual risks**: a `:latest` base means the same role tag can hide a base-image change until the role changes. Also update `docs/runbooks/role-images.md` intro (\"until #449 lands\").\n7. Tests (see Test plan). Run `make lint test`.\n\n### Network inputs\nNone. (The registry check and builds happen at runtime in the cluster; the worker needs no download. Tests use `httptest` and the fake kube client.)\n\n### Test plan\nTest command: `make lint test` (`go test ./internal/executor/... ./internal/servecmd/...` for a quick loop).\n- `internal/executor/kube/roleimage_test.go` (new), with the fake client, a fake git runner and an `httptest` registry:\n  - TagStable: same tree gives same tag; changing a file, a mode, the Dockerfile or `AgentBase` changes it; file order does not.\n  - CachedSkipsBuild: registry HEAD returns 200 plus digest, so no pod or Secret is created and `h.Image` is `<repo>@<digest>`.\n  - BuildSuccess: HEAD 404, builder pod created in the build namespace with the exact pinned shape (image, uid, SA, Secret mounts, `activeDeadlineSeconds`, no `imagePullSecrets`), scripted Succeeded with a digest, pod and Secret deleted, ref returned.\n  - PrivatePackage401: token or HEAD returns 401, so it builds.\n  - RegistryDown: HEAD 500 fails with a `registry check` cause and builds nothing.\n  - BuildFailure: Failed with exit code 1 and logs, so the error names the exit code and log tail, secrets in logs redacted.\n  - BuildTimeout: pod stays Running past a short `Budget`, so the error says timed out and the pod is deleted.\n  - AdmissionDenied: `CreatePod` returns an error, so the error says the builder was refused and the Secret is removed.\n  - BadDigest: termination message without a valid sha256 digest fails.\n  - SingleFlight: two concurrent Prepare calls for one role create one builder pod.\n  - ContextFromSHA: the archive and the tag come from `RoleSource.SHA`, not from `j.RoleDir` or the worktree (create a differing file in `RoleDir`; it must not appear).\n  - Rejects: symlink in the role dir, missing Dockerfile, oversize context, bad role path segments.\n- `kube_test.go`: Prepare with a Dockerfile and `RoleImages == nil` still logs `kube.dockerfile_ignored` and uses `AgentImage`; with it set, the agent container image is the digest ref and `PodImage` is still used for the init/result containers (`pod_test.go`); a build failure leaves no live job and no worktree.\n- `internal/servecmd/k8s_test.go`: env/flags map to `RoleImages`; build namespace unset keeps images off; partial settings or a non-digest builder image give an error.\n- `internal/executor/local`: `docker build` args include `--build-arg AGENT_IMAGE=` only when set.\n- Edge: Dockerfile role with no network access to ghcr, push credential Secret missing (builder pod stays Pending: covered by the build budget).\n\n### Risk\nMedium. New outward network use (registry check) and a new pod type holding the push credential; the controller token can already create these (#448 residual risk) and this adds the code path. No migrations, no concurrency beyond one single-flight map, no change to `deploy/` expected (builder RBAC already exists; if the worker finds the Role needs more, that is under `merge.protected_paths` and needs a human). `docs/proposal.md` and Go code are not protected paths. Recorded residual risk: `:latest` base hides base changes under an unchanged tag.\n\n### Size\nL (about 800 to 1,200 changed lines including tests). Files: `internal/executor/kube/roleimage.go` (new), `roleimage_test.go` (new), `kube.go`, `pod.go` (if needed), `pod_test.go`, `kube_test.go`, `api/types.go`, `api/fake/fake.go`, `internal/servecmd/serve.go`, `internal/servecmd/k8s_test.go`, `internal/executor/local/docker.go` and its test, `docs/proposal.md`, `docs/runbooks/role-images.md`.\nEOF\ncat > .ard/449/triage-engineer.md <<'EOF'\n---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nAdds in-cluster role image builds to the Kubernetes executor: a content-hash tag taken from the role directory at the pinned commit, a registry check, a budgeted builder pod, and a job pod pinned to the image digest. It also passes the agent base as a build arg on the Docker executor and updates the proposal. Size L, risk medium.\n\n## Open issues\n- The builder from #448 is a pod shape enforced by an admission policy, not a batch Job, so the plan builds with a pod.\n- Role Dockerfiles already take the agent base through an `AGENT_IMAGE` build arg, so the plan passes the `:latest` ghcr base as that arg instead of editing their `FROM` lines.\n- If the builder needs more RBAC than the chart grants, that change is under `deploy/`, which is a protected path and needs a human.\n- A private package looks the same as a missing one to the registry check, so the first build of each role is repeated until the package is made public.\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":933,"cache_read_input_tokens":37740,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":933},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f535f0b-91e2-4cd6-a20e-142f0e47e2e5","uuid":"5a59452f-fa62-4090-9c87-6fd6dd155aac","timestamp":"2026-11-26T08:34:52.091Z","request_id":"req_011ChREP6ZteaGJ2V5BqSSh2"}
