{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChREScWoTy6W4GE9Jqz2B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the plan for #449 to `.ard/449/plan.md` and the role file to `.ard/449/triage-engineer.md`, with status `done`. It is size L and medium risk. I haven't built it or run any tests.\n\n**What the plan covers**\n- **Tag:** each image is tagged `h-<hash>`, from a hash of the role directory at the pinned role SHA. The hash input also includes the base build-arg value, so changing the agent base rebuilds.\n- **Source:** the context comes from `git ls-tree` and `git archive` on the controller clone, never from the PR worktree.\n- **Registry check:** the controller makes an anonymous token request and a HEAD on the manifest. A 200 gives the digest and skips the build, and 401, 403 or 404 means build.\n- **Build:** a builder pod in the build namespace, with the context passed in a Secret. It runs under a time budget, and failures give a clear cause. Concurrent builds of the same role share one build.\n- **Pod image:** the job pod runs the image by digest. If no build settings are set, the executor keeps logging `kube.dockerfile_ignored` as before.\n- **Local executor:** it passes `--build-arg AGENT_IMAGE=<local agent image>` when one is configured.\n- **Docs:** the plan updates `docs/proposal.md` and the runbook, and records the `:latest` base risk in the proposal.\n- **Code touched:** the plan also edits `servecmd` to read the build settings, and `api/types.go` and the fake client for test support.\n\n**Differences from the issue**\n- **Pod, not a Job:** the #448 builder is a pod shape enforced by an admission policy, not a batch Job, so the plan builds with a pod.\n- **Base build arg:** role Dockerfiles already take their base through `ARG AGENT_IMAGE`, so the plan passes the `:latest` ghcr base as that arg instead of editing any `FROM` line.\n\n**Open points**\n- **RBAC:** if the builder needs more RBAC than #448 grants, that change is under `deploy/`, a protected path that needs a human.\n- **Private packages:** a private package looks the same as a missing one to the registry check. Until each package is made public, its first build repeats on every job.\n- **Network inputs:** none are needed. Tests use `httptest` and the fake kube client."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6613,"cache_read_input_tokens":38673,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6613},"output_tokens":727,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f535f0b-91e2-4cd6-a20e-142f0e47e2e5","uuid":"8b78af87-9d67-49f8-b0a4-a8f63a495669","timestamp":"2026-11-26T08:34:58.063Z","request_id":"req_011ChREScDguFFhQzQWjo3zX"}
